    "result_text": "All 16 tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a `selfLink` field (`/api/owners/{id}`) to the owner response. Two small, well-placed edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema. Since `OwnerDto` is code-generated from this spec at build time, this creates the field (getter/setter) on the DTO.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression populating `selfLink` from `owner.getId()`, right alongside the existing `displayName` mapping.\n\nThe mapper is the correct home for this: `selfLink` is a pure API-link (HATEOAS) concern derived from the id, not domain state \u2014 exactly like the existing `displayName`, which is also computed in the mapper rather than on the entity. Every `OwnerDto` response flows through `toOwnerDto`, so a single line covers GET, POST, and PUT responses with no duplication and no bloat on the `Owner` entity.\n\nThe `coreReturnsSelfLink` acceptance test passes, and the full suite is green (16/16).",
